  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, has died after an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Paralysed from the chest down in a 2007 riding accident, she became widely known for fundraising and athletic achievements using a bionic suit, including completing the 2012 London Marathon over 17 days and the 2016 Great North Run over five days while pregnant. She raised nearly £1 million for charity and was also chosen to light the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square in 2012. Her family said they were devastated and asked for privacy."
}
```

